      "dcDescription": [
        "1927.27.1273 Cueptí, San Blas-kusten, Panamá Cuepti, San Blas, Panamá. [[Haga]] Bild Cuna Mellanamerika Centralamerika Stag 29 cm hylla 2 Panamá Amerika Expedition till Panama och Colombia (1927) Panama Guna People Guna Cuna Wooden ritual figure from Cuepti Island, made of rosewood from old-growth forests on the mainland. The figure was employed in healing rituals, accompanied by special songs. Once it had served its purpose, it was later used for play, as a doll. Some wooden sculptures were made solely for a specific event or situation. Once it was over, the sculpture would either be disposed"
